   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Regular pattern and irregularity",
     "texto": [
      "Regular verbs follow fixed patterns: **parlare → parlato**, **credere → creduto**, **dormire → dormito**. The verb **dare** has a regular past participle: **dato** (**ho dato il libro a Marco**).",
      "Many verbs of the second conjugation (-ere) have irregular past participles ending in **-to** or **-so**: **prendere → preso**, **mettere → messo**, **leggere → letto**, **chiudere → chiuso**, **aprire → aperto**, **scrivere → scritto**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Consistency in conversation",
     "texto": [
      "In a past-tense narrative, regular and irregular verbs are constantly mixed. Make sure you remember the combination of auxiliary and past participle for each one."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
